      "oracle_independence_basis": "Independent whole-number decimal specification: interpret a nonempty big-endian digit list as a number, add one, decompose the whole result by divmod and left-pad to the original minimum width. This differs from the target per-index carry loop and does not copy its fixed patch. Leading-zero width is an explicit source-inferred bounded contract: original sibling plus_one_v1/v2 and the selected v3 return branches retain list width except overflow, rather than an unconditional upstream prose promise. Inputs such as0,0 remain in-domain and yield0,1; no hidden no-leading-zero precondition is assumed. Source-derived exposed witness1 is frozen before OCI; no target was run to select it. Semantic fidelity outside this stated scope is not established.",
